        "subject": "LU-21123 obdclass: initialize remainder in scale64_rem()",
        "message": "LU-21123 obdclass: initialize remainder in scale64_rem()\n\n- scale64_rem() returns early for a zero base and leaves *remp\n  unset.\n- __string_to_size() adds that remainder for a percentage with a\n  zero integer part, such as \"0%\", \"0.5%\" or \".5%\". The parsed\n  size then depends on stack contents.\n- Callers with percentages: llite max_read_ahead_mb,\n  max_read_ahead_per_file_mb, max_read_ahead_whole_mb,\n  max_cached_mb and lod dom_threshold_free_mb.\n- obd_init_checks() parses \"0%\", \"0.5%\" and \".5%\" at load. A stale\n  value of 100 or more fails a check, and obdclass does not load.\n- Set *remp to zero on the zero-base return.\n\nTest-Parameters: trivial\nFixes: f62e51414712 (\"LU-18163 obdclass: add sysfs_memparse_total() string helper\")\nSigned-off-by: Andreas Krause <akrause@nvidia.com>\nChange-Id: I78770a70a397683b7454c1810aec2502855d9fc0\n"
      },
      "branch": "refs/heads/master"
    }
